Reference quirk. `\fqa ... drink. \fv 38\fv*\ft ...`: the hand-written USX
nests `\fv` inside `\fqa`, but the stylesheet does not let `\fqa` hold nested
styles (no `NEST` in its `OccursUnder`), and Paratext writes the same shape
as a sibling in paratextTests (`\ft ... \fqa ...\fqa*`). The parser closes
`\fqa` at `\fv`.

